b</span><span>=C2=B7</span><span>2026-04-28</span></div></header><img src=
=3D"https://ffhub.io/imgs/blog/how-to-add-subtitles-to-video-with-ffmpeg.we=
bp" alt=3D"How to Add Subtitles to Video with FFmpeg" class=3D"mb-8 w-full =
rounded-lg object-cover"><div class=3D"space-y-2"><p class=3D"my-4 leading-=
relaxed">Subtitles make videos accessible, searchable, and watchable in noi=
sy environments. FFmpeg can hardcode subtitles directly into the video, emb=
ed them as selectable tracks, extract existing subtitles, and convert betwe=
en subtitle formats. This guide covers all of it with practical commands.</=
p>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Hardcode vs Softcode: Which to Ch=
oose?</h2>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">Before adding subtitles, you need to deci=
de how:</p>
<table class=3D"my-4 w-full border-collapse text-sm"><thead><tr><th class=
=3D"border border-foreground/20 bg-foreground/5 px-3 py-2 text-left">Method=
</th><th class=3D"border border-foreground/20 bg-foreground/5 px-3 py-2 tex=
t-left">Description</th><th class=3D"border border-foreground/20 bg-foregro=
und/5 px-3 py-2 text-left">Pros</th><th class=3D"border border-foreground/2=
0 bg-foreground/5 px-3 py-2 text-left">Cons</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td=
 class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2"><strong>Hardcode</strong> =
(burn-in)</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Subtitles=
 rendered into the video pixels</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/2=
0 px-3 py-2">Always visible, universal playback</td><td class=3D"border bor=
der-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Can't turn off, requires re-encoding</td></tr>=
<tr><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2"><strong>Softcode</s=
trong> (embedded)</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">S=
ubtitles stored as a separate track</td><td class=3D"border border-foregrou=
nd/20 px-3 py-2">Toggleable, multiple languages</td><td class=3D"border bor=
der-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Player must support it</td></tr></tbody></tabl=
e>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed"><strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> Hardcode =
for social media and maximum compatibility. Softcode for long-form content =
and multi-language support. If you're building a <a class=3D"text-blue-600 =
underline hover:text-blue-800" href=3D"https://ffhub.io/blog/video-processi=
ng-for-ugc-platforms">UGC platform that processes user-uploaded videos</a>,=
 softcode is usually the better choice.</p>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Hardcode SRT Subtitles</h2>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">SRT is the most common subtitle format. T=
o burn it into the video:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Hardcode SRT subtitles
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt" output.mp4
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">That's it. FFmpeg uses the <code class=3D=
"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">subtitles</code> f=
ilter (powered by libass) to render the SRT file directly onto each frame.<=
/p>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Customize SRT Appearance</h3>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">The default SRT rendering is plain. You c=
an style it with the <code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 fo=
nt-mono text-sm">force_style</code> option:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Custom font, size, and color
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt:force_style=3D'FontName=3DAri=
al,FontSize=3D24,PrimaryColour=3D&amp;H00FFFFFF,OutlineColour=3D&amp;H00000=
000,Outline=3D2,Shadow=3D1'" output.mp4
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">Common style parameters:</p>
<table class=3D"my-4 w-full border-collapse text-sm"><thead><tr><th class=
=3D"border border-foreground/20 bg-foreground/5 px-3 py-2 text-left">Parame=
ter</th><th class=3D"border border-foreground/20 bg-foreground/5 px-3 py-2 =
text-left">Example</th><th class=3D"border border-foreground/20 bg-foregrou=
nd/5 px-3 py-2 text-left">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=
=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">FontName</td><td class=3D"border=
 border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Arial</td><td class=3D"border border-foreg=
round/20 px-3 py-2">Font face</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border border-foreg=
round/20 px-3 py-2">FontSize</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 p=
x-3 py-2">24</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Size i=
n points</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">P=
rimaryColour</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">&amp;H=
00FFFFFF</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Text color=
 (ABGR hex)</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2=
">OutlineColour</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">&am=
p;H00000000</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Outline=
 color</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Bac=
kColour</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">&amp;H80000=
000</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Shadow/backgrou=
nd color</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">O=
utline</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">2</td><td cl=
ass=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Outline thickness</td></tr><t=
r><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Shadow</td><td class=
=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">1</td><td class=3D"border border=
-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Shadow depth</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border bor=
der-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Bold</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground=
/20 px-3 py-2">1</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Bo=
ld text (0 or 1)</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3=
 py-2">Alignment</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">2<=
/td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Position (2=3Dbotto=
m center)</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">=
MarginV</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">30</td><td =
class=3D"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Vertical margin from edge</=
td></tr></tbody></table>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">Note: Colors use <strong>ABGR</strong> fo=
rmat (Alpha, Blue, Green, Red), not the usual RGB.</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Yellow text with black outline, larger font, positioned h=
igher
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt:force_style=3D'FontSize=3D28,=
PrimaryColour=3D&amp;H0000FFFF,OutlineColour=3D&amp;H00000000,Outline=3D3,M=
arginV=3D40'" output.mp4
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Handle Special Characters in File =
Paths</h3>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">If your subtitle file path contains speci=
al characters, escape them:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Escape colons in Windows paths or special characters
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3D'my\ subtitles.srt'" output.mp4

# Or use the subtitle file index approach
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -i subs.srt -filter_complex "[0:v][1:s]overlay" output.=
mp4
</code></pre>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Hardcode ASS/SSA Styled Subtitles=
</h2>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">ASS (Advanced SubStation Alpha) subtitles=
 support rich styling =E2=80=94 fonts, colors, animations, and positioning =
per line. When hardcoding ASS files, all styling is preserved:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Hardcode ASS subtitles (all styling preserved)
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "ass=3Dsubs.ass" output.mp4
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Create a Simple ASS File</h3>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">Here's an example ASS file structure:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-text">[Script Info]
Title: My Subtitles
ScriptType: v4.00+
PlayResX: 1920
PlayResY: 1080

[V4+ Styles]
Format: Name, Fontname, Fontsize, PrimaryColour, SecondaryColour, OutlineCo=
lour, BackColour, Bold, Italic, Underline, StrikeOut, ScaleX, ScaleY, Spaci=
ng, Angle, BorderStyle, Outline, Shadow, Alignment, MarginL, MarginR, Margi=
nV, Encoding
Style: Default,Arial,48,&amp;H00FFFFFF,&amp;H000000FF,&amp;H00000000,&amp;H=
80000000,0,0,0,0,100,100,0,0,1,2,1,2,10,10,40,1

[Events]
Format: Layer, Start, End, Style, Name, MarginL, MarginR, MarginV, Effect, =
Text
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.00,0:00:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello, this is a subtitle=
.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.00,0:00:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This line has {\b1}bold{\=
b0} text.
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Convert SRT to ASS with Custom Sty=
ling</h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Convert SRT to ASS (then you can edit the ASS styles)
ffmpeg -i subs.srt subs.ass
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">After converting, edit the <code class=3D=
"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">[V4+ Styles]</code=
> section in the ASS file to customize appearance. You may also want to <a =
class=3D"text-blue-600 underline hover:text-blue-800" href=3D"https://ffhub=
.io/blog/how-to-convert-video-format-with-ffmpeg">convert your video to a d=
ifferent format</a> before adding subtitles, depending on your target platf=
orm.</p>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Softcode Subtitles (Embedded Trac=
ks)</h2>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">Softcoded subtitles are stored as a separ=
ate stream inside the container. The viewer can toggle them on/off.</p>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Add SRT as a Subtitle Track</h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Add SRT subtitle track to MP4
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -i subs.srt -c copy -c:s mov_text output.mp4

# Add SRT subtitle track to MKV (MKV supports SRT natively)
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -i subs.srt -c copy -c:s srt output.mkv
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">Important: MP4 containers require <code c=
lass=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">mov_text</c=
ode> codec for subtitles. MKV supports SRT, ASS, and many other formats nat=
ively.</p>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Add Multiple Subtitle Languages</h=
3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Add English and Spanish subtitle tracks to MKV
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -i english.srt -i spanish.srt \
  -map 0:v -map 0:a -map 1 -map 2 \
  -c copy -c:s srt \
  -metadata:s:s:0 language=3Deng -metadata:s:s:0 title=3D"English" \
  -metadata:s:s:1 language=3Dspa -metadata:s:s:1 title=3D"Spanish" \
  output.mkv
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">For MP4:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Add multiple subtitle tracks to MP4
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -i english.srt -i chinese.srt \
  -map 0:v -map 0:a -map 1 -map 2 \
  -c copy -c:s mov_text \
  -metadata:s:s:0 language=3Deng -metadata:s:s:0 title=3D"English" \
  -metadata:s:s:1 language=3Dchi -metadata:s:s:1 title=3D"Chinese" \
  output.mp4
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Set Default Subtitle Track</h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Mark the first subtitle track as default
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -i subs.srt \
  -map 0 -map 1 \
  -c copy -c:s mov_text \
  -disposition:s:0 default \
  output.mp4
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Add ASS Subtitles as Soft Track</h=
3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Add ASS to MKV (preserves all styling for compatible play=
ers)
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -i subs.ass -map 0 -map 1 -c copy -c:s ass output.mkv
</code></pre>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Extract Subtitles from Video</h2>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Extract to SRT</h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Extract the first subtitle track to SRT
ffmpeg -i input.mkv -map 0:s:0 output.srt

# Extract the second subtitle track
ffmpeg -i input.mkv -map 0:s:1 output.srt
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Extract to ASS</h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Extract subtitle track as ASS (preserves styling)
ffmpeg -i input.mkv -map 0:s:0 output.ass
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">List Available Subtitle Tracks</h3=
>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Show all streams including subtitles
ffprobe -v error -show_entries stream=3Dindex,codec_name,codec_type -of csv=
 input.mkv

# More detailed subtitle info
ffprobe -v error -select_streams s -show_entries stream=3Dindex,codec_name:=
stream_tags=3Dlanguage,title -of json input.mkv
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Extract All Subtitle Tracks</h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash">#!/bin/bash
# Extract all subtitle tracks from a video
INPUT=3D"input.mkv"

# Count subtitle streams
COUNT=3D$(ffprobe -v error -select_streams s -show_entries stream=3Dindex -=
of csv=3Dp=3D0 "$INPUT" | wc -l)

for i in $(seq 0 $((COUNT - 1))); do
  # Get language tag
  LANG=3D$(ffprobe -v error -select_streams s:$i -show_entries stream_tags=
=3Dlanguage -of csv=3Dp=3D0 "$INPUT")
  LANG=3D${LANG:-"track$i"}
  ffmpeg -i "$INPUT" -map 0:s:$i "${INPUT%.*}_${LANG}.srt"
done
</code></pre>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Convert Subtitle Formats</h2>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">FFmpeg can convert between subtitle forma=
ts:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># SRT to ASS
ffmpeg -i subs.srt subs.ass

# ASS to SRT (loses styling)
ffmpeg -i subs.ass subs.srt

# SRT to WebVTT
ffmpeg -i subs.srt subs.vtt

# SUB/IDX (DVD) to SRT (requires OCR =E2=80=94 FFmpeg can't do this directl=
y)
# Use a tool like SubtitleEdit or Tesseract for bitmap-to-text conversion
</code></pre>
<table class=3D"my-4 w-full border-collapse text-sm"><thead><tr><th class=
=3D"border border-foreground/20 bg-foreground/5 px-3 py-2 text-left">From</=
th><th class=3D"border border-foreground/20 bg-foreground/5 px-3 py-2 text-=
left">To</th><th class=3D"border border-foreground/20 bg-foreground/5 px-3 =
py-2 text-left">Preserves Styling?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=3D=
"border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">SRT =E2=86=92 ASS</td><td class=3D"=
border border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Yes</td><td class=3D"border border-f=
oreground/20 px-3 py-2">Adds default styling</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"bord=
er border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">ASS =E2=86=92 SRT</td><td class=3D"borde=
r border-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">No</td><td class=3D"border border-foregro=
und/20 px-3 py-2">Loses all styling</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border border=
-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">SRT =E2=86=92 VTT</td><td class=3D"border border-=
foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Partial</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/=
20 px-3 py-2">Basic formatting kept</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border border=
-foreground/20 px-3 py-2">VTT =E2=86=92 SRT</td><td class=3D"border border-=
foreground/20 px-3 py-2">Partial</td><td class=3D"border border-foreground/=
20 px-3 py-2">Loses VTT-specific features</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Subtitle Timing Adjustments</h2>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Delay or Advance Subtitles</h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Delay subtitles by 2.5 seconds
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -itsoffset 2.5 -i subs.srt -map 0 -map 1 -c copy -c:s m=
ov_text output.mp4
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">For hardcoded subtitles, use the <code cl=
ass=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">setpts</code=
> filter or adjust the SRT file directly (if you need to <a class=3D"text-b=
lue-600 underline hover:text-blue-800" href=3D"https://ffhub.io/blog/how-to=
-trim-and-merge-videos-with-ffmpeg">trim or merge video segments</a>, timin=
g adjustments become especially important):</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Shift hardcoded subtitles (using subtitle filter with off=
set)
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt" -ss 00:00:02.500 output.mp4
</code></pre>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Hardcode Subtitles with Resolutio=
n Control</h2>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">When hardcoding, subtitle rendering quali=
ty depends on the video resolution. For best results, match the original re=
solution:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Hardcode subtitles while keeping original resolution
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt" -c:v libx264 -crf 23 -c:a co=
py output.mp4

# Hardcode and scale to 1080p
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt,scale=3D-2:1080" -c:v libx264=
 -crf 23 -c:a copy output.mp4
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Subtitle Font Rendering for Differ=
ent Resolutions</h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># For 720p video =E2=80=94 smaller font
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt:force_style=3D'FontSize=3D20'=
" -c:v libx264 -crf 23 output.mp4

# For 4K video =E2=80=94 larger font
ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt:force_style=3D'FontSize=3D48,=
Outline=3D3'" -c:v libx264 -crf 23 output.mp4
</code></pre>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Batch Subtitle Operations</h2>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Hardcode Subtitles for All Videos<=
/h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Assumes each video has a matching .srt file
for f in *.mp4; do
  srt=3D"${f%.mp4}.srt"
  if [ -f "$srt" ]; then
    ffmpeg -i "$f" -vf "subtitles=3D$srt" -c:v libx264 -crf 23 -c:a copy "s=
ubtitled_${f}"
  fi
done
</code></pre>
<h3 class=3D"mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Softcode Subtitles for All Videos<=
/h3>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Add matching SRT files as subtitle tracks
for f in *.mp4; do
  srt=3D"${f%.mp4}.srt"
  if [ -f "$srt" ]; then
    ffmpeg -i "$f" -i "$srt" -c copy -c:s mov_text "soft_${f}"
  fi
done
</code></pre>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Troubleshooting</h2>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed"><strong>"No such filter: subtitles"</stro=
ng> =E2=80=94 FFmpeg was compiled without libass support. Install a full bu=
ild:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># macOS
brew install ffmpeg

# Ubuntu/Debian
sudo apt install ffmpeg libass-dev
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed"><strong>Subtitles don't appear</strong> =
=E2=80=94 Check the subtitle file encoding. FFmpeg expects UTF-8:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash"># Convert subtitle encoding to UTF-8
iconv -f ISO-8859-1 -t UTF-8 subs_latin.srt &gt; subs_utf8.srt
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed"><strong>Wrong subtitle position or size</=
strong> =E2=80=94 The video resolution doesn't match the subtitle's assumed=
 resolution. Use <code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-m=
ono text-sm">force_style</code> to override:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash">ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt:force_style=
=3D'FontSize=3D24,MarginV=3D30'" output.mp4
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed"><strong>Special characters display as box=
es</strong> =E2=80=94 The font doesn't support the characters. Specify a fo=
nt that supports your language:</p>
<pre class=3D"my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-foreground/5 p-4 font-mono=
 text-sm [&amp;>code]:bg-transparent [&amp;>code]:p-0 [&amp;>code]:text-inh=
erit"><code class=3D"rounded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm=
 language-bash">ffmpeg -i input.mp4 -vf "subtitles=3Dsubs.srt:force_style=
=3D'FontName=3DNoto Sans CJK SC'" output.mp4
</code></pre>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed"><strong>MP4 output fails with "unknown co=
dec" for subtitles</strong> =E2=80=94 MP4 only supports <code class=3D"roun=
ded bg-foreground/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">mov_text</code>. Use MK=
V for other subtitle formats, or hardcode instead.</p>
<h2 class=3D"mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold">Cloud Alternative with FFHub</h2>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">Hardcoding subtitles requires re-encoding=
, which is CPU-intensive =E2=80=94 a 1-hour video can take 20+ minutes on a=
 standard machine. <a class=3D"text-blue-600 underline hover:text-blue-800"=
 href=3D"https://ffhub.io/">FFHub</a> runs FFmpeg in the cloud via API, so =
you can offload subtitle burning to fast cloud servers while your machine s=
tays free.</p>
<p class=3D"my-4 leading-relaxed">This is especially useful when you need t=
o generate multiple subtitle versions (different languages, different style=
s) from the same source video.</p>
